- `data/inference_test/results/opus-5-5.csv` and `results/sonnet-5-5.csv`
- `data/inference_test/logs/opus-5-5_log.csv` and `logs/sonnet-5-5_log.csv`
- `data/inference_test/logs/opus-5-5_check.csv` and `logs/sonnet-5-5_check.csv`

Step 1 is ready for both models; commit first if you want the git hash in the run line. This run uses all the new rules:
- the 36 columns;
- FRR back to `resprouter`;
- `fire_response_implied`;
- the error and sample size columns;
- `supplementary_material`;
- post-fire rainfall.

When the runs are done, I'll check:
- the benchmark against the last 2 runs;
- the new columns by hand: errors in Knox, Muir and Miller; supplements in wf24046 and Miller; implied fire responses;
- token use, since more columns may cost more.

